.TH OPENDIALCTL 1 "2026-11-10" "OpenDial 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opendialctl \- control and inspect the OpenDial Surface Dial service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opendialctl
[\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opendialctl
talks to
.BR opendiald (1)
over the session D-Bus API. With \fB\-\-json\fR every command prints machine-readable JSON.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Status
.TP
.B status
Device, battery, haptics, active profile and tool, injection and focus capabilities.
.TP
.B diagnose \fR[\fB\-\-export\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-redact\fR]
Full diagnostic report. Redacted by default (no Bluetooth addresses, window titles or paths).
Exported files are written with mode 0600 inside your home, /tmp or the runtime directory only.
.TP
.B devices
Surface Dial input and hidraw nodes and whether they are accessible.
.TP
.B watch \fR[\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-\-seconds\fR \fIN\fR]
Stream gesture (and raw evdev) events as JSON lines.
.TP
.B record \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-seconds\fR \fIN\fR]
Record raw events to a replay fixture.
.SS Tools and profiles
.TP
.B tools
Tools in the current radial menu.
.TP
.B tool \fIID\fR
Make \fIID\fR the active tool.
.TP
.B profiles
List profiles.
.TP
.B profile lock \fR[\fIID\fR] | \fBunlock\fR
Pin a profile regardless of the focused app.
.TP
.B menu open\fR|\fBclose
Show or hide the radial menu.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config path\fR|\fBget\fR|\fBvalidate \fR[\fIFILE\fR]|\fBset \fIFILE\fR|\fBreset\fR|\fBrollback
\fBvalidate\fR works without the service. \fBrollback\fR restores the previous configuration; repeat to go further back.
.TP
.B import \fIFILE\fR / \fBexport \fIID\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
Import or export a profile. Imported commands, launches, D-Bus and OSC actions stay disabled until approved.
.TP
.B approvals\fR, \fBapprove \fIFINGERPRINT\fR, \fBrevoke \fIFINGERPRINT\fR
Review and approve actions that run programs or contact other services.
.TP
.B plugins\fR, \fBplugin allow\fR|\fBdeny \fIAPPID\fR
Registered app integrations and their consent.
.SS Device
.TP
.B test haptics \fR[\fBclick\fR|\fBbuzz\fR|\fBrumble\fR]
.TP
.B bluetooth status\fR|\fBdiscover\fR|\fBstop\-discovery\fR|\fBpair\fR|\fBconnect\fR|\fBdisconnect\fR|\fBtrust\fR|\fBremove \fR[\fIPATH\fR]
Pair and manage the Dial through BlueZ.
.TP
.B reconnect\fR, \fBportal\fR, \fBpause\fR, \fBresume
.SS Simulation
.TP
.B simulate click \fR[\fIN\fR] | \fBpress\fR | \fBrelease\fR | \fBlongpress\fR | \fBrotate \fIDEGREES\fR | \fBjson \fI'{...}'\fR
Drive the service without hardware.
.TP
.B context \fIAPPID\fR [\fITITLE\fR] | \fBcontext clear
Pretend an app is focused (profile testing).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error, 3 service not running.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
opendialctl status
opendialctl --json tools
opendialctl simulate longpress; opendialctl simulate rotate 20; opendialctl simulate click
opendialctl diagnose --export ~/opendial-report.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR opendial (1),
.BR opendiald (1)
